ator might reject. But we have no way to know.\n\nAnother possibility: The \"last_trial\" could be the absolute trial number in the entire sequence, which is the index we used. That seems fine.\n\nThus, proceed.\n\nNow, we need to output the entire response as one valid JSON object. So we will output:\n\n{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    capacity = case['capacity']\\n    trials = case['trials']\\n    memory = []\\n    seen_signatures = []\\n    seen_set = set()\\n    for idx, trial in enumerate(trials):\\n        item = {\\n            'last_trial': idx,\\n            'reflection': trial['reflection'],\\n            'signature': trial['signature'],\\n            'success': trial['success']\\n        }\\n        memory.append(item)\\n        if len(memory) > capacity:\\n            memory.pop(0)\\n        sig = trial['signature']\\n        if sig not in seen_set:\\n            seen_set.add(sig)\\n            seen_signatures.append(sig)\\n    return {\\n        'memory': memory,\\n        'signatures': seen_signatures\\n    }\"}\n\nMake sure there is no trailing comma or extra whitespace. The JSON must be valid.\n\nI'll produce that."},"logprobs":null,"finish_reason":"stop"}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":1453,"completion_tokens":5787,"total_tokens":7240,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0},"completion_tokens_details":{"reasoning_tokens":5589},"prompt_cache_hit_tokens":0,"prompt_cache_miss_tokens":1453},"system_fingerprint":"fp_8b330d02d0_prod0820_fp8_kvcache_20260402"}